{
  "about": "Per-control specimens from the design (tools/fidelity/README.md, Specimens). lib/specimen.mjs expands each control into ordinary scenes: one still per state (`spec-<control>--<state>`, a tight crop: the union of `root` and the state's `clip` selectors plus `pad` px) and one frame burst per sequence (`spec-<control>--seq-<name>`, 1/120 s per frame, with curve.json of the `track` elements). `{root}` in a selector or step is replaced by the control's root. `page` names a page below; `before` runs after the page's steps (for settings: a search that brings the row to the top). `elements` are the named parts whose rects (<id>.rects.json) and curves the controls lanes compare against wubble (geometry-diff.mjs). `source` is a design `@source` anchor or `path#text` (first line containing text), resolved to file:line in specimens-index.json. States are only those the design defines; `after` (ms on the fixed clock after the steps) defaults to the page's. The settings page settles the liquid only 100 ms: every settings specimen lies inside the page's opaque `.wb-main-in`, so the liquid never shows in it (SwiftShader still draws it: on the GPU these crops differ by 0.6 to 1.0 mean ΔE, so they stay on SwiftShader).",
